  "notes": "{漬|つ}ける means to pickle or soak something in liquid.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を〜に{漬|つ}ける: to soak/pickle X in Y\n- {塩|しお}に{漬|つ}ける: to pickle in salt\n- {酢|す}に{漬|つ}ける: to pickle in vinegar\n- {水|みず}に{漬|つ}ける: to soak in water\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {漬物|つけもの}: pickled vegetables, pickles\n- {漬|つ}け{込|こ}む: to marinate, to soak thoroughly\n- {浸|ひた}す: to soak, to immerse (synonym)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n- Pair: {漬|つ}かる (intransitive - to be soaked)\n\nUSAGE:\nDifferent from {付|つ}ける (00761_tsukeru) which means \"to attach.\"",
